{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b What is copied (review before deploying):}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 All other fields are copied from the source site, including Harbor hostname, TLS certificate/key paths, Harbor secrets, and supervisor sizing. These will reference the source site's values \u8212- update them to match the new environment before saving.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Network segment names:} Segment names are regenerated by appending {\f1 -<new-site-name>} and RFC1123-sanitizing the result. For example, a source segment {\f1 guestnetwork-edge-site-1} becomes {\f1 guestnetwork-edge-site-1-edge-site-2} for a new site named {\f1 edge-site-2}. Supervisor network names (FLB management, virtual-server, management, and workload) are renamed with the same pattern. All segment gateways are cleared and must be entered for the new network.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Supervisor FLB gateways are auto-populated from segments:} In the Supervisor Configuration step, when you select a network segment for {\b FLB Management Network} or {\b FLB Virtual Server Network}, the UI automatically copies that segment's gateway CIDR into the supervisor {\f1 flbNetworkGateway} field and saves it to {\f1 supervisor.json}. This eliminates the need to enter the gateway twice. When loading an existing {\f1 supervisor.json} that contains these values, they are now preserved on save.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Review banner:} Immediately after cloning, a yellow banner on the new site card lists the auto-generated segment names, VMkernel services that need IPs, and a reminder to re-select segments in Supervisor Configuration to auto-populate the FLB gateways. It also shows the auto-computed workload service start IP. Review each item, enter the required values, and dismiss the banner when done.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Note\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Network segment names are matched case-sensitively between {\f1 infrastructure.json} and {\f1 supervisor.json}. Verify that the generated segment names match what is in the supervisor configuration.\par}
