\cell}
{{\pard\intbl \ql \f0 \sa0 \li0 \fi0 Boolean lab mode. JSON property name is case-insensitive; {\b {\f1 labenvironment}} matches {\b {\f1 Templates/infrastructure.json}} and {\b {\f1 Docs/infrastructure-config-help.json}}. Default {\f1 false}. When {\f1 true}, silences the vSAN HCL / hardware-compatibility health checks ({\f1 controlleronhcl}, {\f1 controllerdiskmode}, {\f1 controllerfirmware}, {\f1 controllerdriver}, {\f1 hclhostbadstate}) plus transient {\f1 advcfgsync}, and lab-filters the third-party IO filter alarm. This masks the red vSAN alarm signal but does {\b not} change the underlying hardware state; Supervisor enablement (WCP) still enforces cluster/host HCL conformance downstream, so a cluster that deploys cleanly in lab mode may fail to enable Supervisor outside lab mode on identical hardware. Also permits {\f1 -Force} to bypass cleanup confirmation and allows Harbor self-signed TLS when {\f1 tlsCrt}/{\f1 tlsKey} are both omitted. Keep {\f1 false} for production-equivalent deployments; use {\f1 true} only for nested / demo environments. See the {\b Lab environment and the vSAN HCL} bullet above.\par}
\cell}
}
